GhostWire Wi-Fi — bundled aircrack-ng suite (static aarch64)
============================================================

The Wi-Fi tab runs these as root from the app's own files dir (WifiTools.kt).
They are statically-linked aarch64 Android executables — self-contained, no
shared libraries, no Kali chroot / NetHunter needed. Drop them in assets/wifi/bin
before building a release; the app extracts and chmod's them on first use.

Layout the app expects:

  assets/wifi/bin/            (chmod 755 at runtime)
    airodump-ng   (core)      scan + CSV + pcap capture
    aireplay-ng   (core)      deauth / injection
    aircrack-ng   (core)      key recovery
    iw            (core)      interface enumeration / mode switch
    hcxdumptool   (phase 5)   PMKID capture
    hcxpcapngtool (phase 5)   handshake/PMKID hash export + confirm
    reaver, wash  (phase 5)   WPS pixie / PIN
    bully         (phase 5)   WPS fallback
    pixiewps      (phase 5)   WPS pixie-dust offline

Provenance / build
------------------
Built static for aarch64 Android (bionic, API 21) with the Android NDK using
kimocoder's cross-compile build system:
  https://github.com/kimocoder/kali-nethunter-tools   (GPL-3.0)
    ./docker-build.sh build-image
    ./docker-build.sh build --arch arm64 aircrack-ng iw reaver pixiewps hcxdumptool hcxtools
  binaries land in out/aarch64-linux-android/<tool>/bin/

Versions: aircrack-ng 1.7, iw 6.17, reaver 1.6.6 (t6x), hcxdumptool 7.0.1,
hcxtools 7.0.1, pixiewps 1.4.2.

